> Below is a **5e-style expedition storyboard** for the journey to the Vale of Sleeping Colossi. It assumes a party around **levels 4–6**; reduce enemy numbers for a smaller/younger party, or add one extra foe for a strong group.
> 
> Use the trip as a sequence of scenes, not random encounters. Each scene can grant a benefit, impose a cost, or change who reaches the Vale first.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## Scene 1: The Redclaw Crossing
> 
> **Place:** The ancient road out of Redclaw Cliffs has collapsed into a maze of narrow ledges above a red-rock gorge.
> 
> **Who is there**
> - **Merchant Sela Venn** and her two teenage caravan hands, trapped on the far side with a broken wagon.
> - A small group of **masked scouts** watching from above: servants of the rival relic-seeker, **Captain Vaelor**.
> 
> **What Grima’s map shows:** A giant’s old stepping-stone route across the gorge—but several stones have fallen.
> 
> ### What happens
> The party sees the caravan in trouble. A rope-and-plank crossing has snapped, leaving Sela’s wagon and pack lizard dangerously close to the edge.
> 
> ### Options
> - **Help the caravan.**  
>   - *Athletics DC 13* to secure ropes, *Survival DC 12* to find a safer ledge route, or clever magic/tools.  
>   - **Success:** Sela offers supplies, a sheltered camp location, and a stamped trade-token that earns goodwill with people on the caravan road later. The party loses half a day.  
>   - **Failure:** Someone takes minor falling damage or a supply bundle is lost; they still save the caravan if they persist.
> - **Take Grima’s giant route quickly.**  
>   - *Acrobatics or Athletics DC 14* for the exposed leap-and-climb route.  
>   - **Success:** gain half a day; the scouts do not get a clean look at the party.  
>   - **Failure:** the scouts identify Ekemon and report ahead; Captain Vaelor’s group begins one step closer to the Mouth of Orun.
> - **Confront or ambush the scouts.**  
>   - *Stealth DC 13* to surprise them; *Persuasion/Intimidation DC 14* to force information from one.  
>   - They know only: “The captain wants the thing inside the stone mouth.”
> 
> **Lasting consequence:**  
> Helping Sela grants **1 Supply** and **1 Standing**. Rushing ahead gives **1 Time** advantage but makes the rivals more prepared.
> 
> ### Combat: Redclaw Scouts
> Use 3 scouts, or 4 for a large party.
> 
> **Redclaw Scout**  
> *Medium humanoid, AC 14, HP 18, Speed 30 ft.*  
> - **Shortsword:** +4 to hit, 1d6+2 piercing.  
> - **Light crossbow:** +4 to hit, range 80/320, 1d8+2 piercing.  
> - **Skirmisher:** May Disengage as a bonus action.  
> - **Cowardly Orders:** When half their number falls, the remaining scouts attempt to flee rather than fight to the death.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## Scene 2: Ashfang Pass
> 
> **Place:** A high mountain pass of black volcanic stone. Ash falls like snow. Lightning flickers inside a distant smoke plume.
> 
> **Who is there**
> - **Asha Embervein**, a fire-touched guide and leader among the **Cinderstep Nomads**.
> - Her people are sheltering beneath basalt overhangs.
> - A wounded **ash drake** is panicking nearby after being trapped under a fallen slab.
> 
> ### What happens
> An ash storm will close the pass by nightfall. Asha knows three ways through, but will not guide strangers for free.
> 
> ### Options
> - **Earn Asha’s trust by helping the ash drake.**  
>   The creature is frightened, not evil.  
>   - *Animal Handling DC 14* to calm it; *Medicine DC 13* or *Athletics DC 15* to free it.  
>   - **Success:** Asha guides the party through protected lava tubes. They avoid the storm and gain **1 Resolve**. The drake may later recognize Ekemon.  
>   - **Failure:** the drake attacks briefly, then flees at half HP.
> - **Bargain with the nomads.**  
>   Offer supplies, a favor, information about Grima, or assistance with a local problem.  
>   - *Persuasion DC 14*, with advantage for a meaningful offer.  
>   - **Success:** safe passage and a pouch of ember-salt: one use, grants resistance to fire damage for one hour to up to four creatures.
> - **Take the high route alone.**  
>   - Group *Survival DC 14* to navigate, then *Constitution save DC 13* against choking ash.  
>   - **Success:** fast route; arrive at the Waystation before Vaelor.  
>   - **Failure:** lose supplies and arrive exhausted: each character begins the next scene with one fewer Hit Die or similar system-appropriate fatigue.
> - **Descend into Titan tunnels.**  
>   This route is safe from the storm but has old defenses and strange echoes.  
>   - *Investigation DC 13* to avoid a pressure plate; *History/Arcana DC 14* reveals Titan symbols that foreshadow the Voice.  
>   - **Success:** discover an inscription: *“Strength that speaks only of itself becomes a landslide.”*  
>   - **Failure:** awaken ash mephits or trigger a minor cave-in.
> 
> ### Combat: Frightened Ash Drake
> Use only if the rescue goes badly or the party attacks it.
> 
> **Young Ash Drake**  
> *Medium dragon, AC 14, HP 45, Speed 30 ft., fly 50 ft.*  
> - **Bite:** +5 to hit, 1d8+3 piercing plus 1d6 fire.  
> - **Cinder Breath (Recharge 5–6):** 15-foot cone, DC 13 Dexterity save, 4d6 fire damage; half on success.  
> - **Frightened Animal:** If reduced below 22 HP, it flees unless cornered.
> 
> ### Combat: Ash Mephits
> Use 3–5 if the party chooses the tunnels and triggers a defense.
> 
> **Ash Mephit**  
> *Small elemental, AC 12, HP 10, fly 30 ft.*  
> - **Claws:** +3 to hit, 1d4+1 slashing plus 1d4 fire.  
> - **Ash Breath (Recharge 6):** 15-foot cone, DC 10 Dexterity save, 2d6 fire; half on success.  
> - **Death Burst:** creatures within 5 ft. make DC 10 Dexterity save or take 1d4 fire.
> 
