>   - **Success:** the forest grants the party **Greenwarden’s Passage**: they may safely rest once in the Vale and cannot be tracked there by ordinary means. Gain **1 Resolve**.  
>   - **Failure:** the Briar lashes out; the party still may proceed, but the wardens will not support them.
> - **Promise help later and press on.**  
>   - *Persuasion DC 15* to avoid offending the wardens.  
>   - **Success:** they reluctantly reveal the quickest route, but do not grant their blessing.  
>   - **Failure:** they bar the direct path, adding one day or forcing the dangerous marsh approach.
> - **Attempt to command the forest with Titan power.**  
>   Ekemon may use the Seed, Plate, or Heartshard.  
>   - *Charisma or Wisdom save DC 15.*  
>   - **Success:** the forest yields—but uneasily. Gain speed, lose **1 Standing**.  
>   - **Failure:** the Briar senses the power and becomes more dangerous. This should feel effective but ethically troubling.
> 
